# Copy to `.dev.vars` for `wrangler pages dev` (never commit real secrets).
# In Cloudflare Pages, set these as production secrets / environment variables.

# Optional origin JWT verification (defense in depth) for Cloudflare Access.
# When both are unset, Pages Functions pass requests through so local
# `wrangler pages dev` and a site already behind Access keep working.
# Production still relies on the Access application in front of
# recipes.palko.dev (email one-time PIN).
#
# CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN is your Cloudflare One team domain, for example:
#   your-team.cloudflareaccess.com
# JWKS is fetched from:
#   https://<team>.cloudflareaccess.com/cdn-cgi/access/certs
# CF_ACCESS_AUD is the Application Audience (AUD) tag from
#   Zero Trust → Access → Applications → recipes.palko.dev
# CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=
# CF_ACCESS_AUD=

# Family recipes and photos are stored in an R2 bucket bound as RECIPES
# (see wrangler.jsonc). Create it with:
#   pnpm wrangler r2 bucket create theisen-recipes
